# `show(sheet.title, sheet.rows)` is handed the sheet, through two projections: inside `show`, `title` and `rows` hold
# it, each by the place its argument is written in (#157), so the loop goes over the sheet, and `print(title, ..)` reads
# it. A parameter the plan cannot pair with what its call hands still holds no value from beyond the route: it is a
# value of the body whose parameter it is, made by no step the plan follows, in that body's frame (#159). Closed, `show`
# takes no `Row` from beyond.

route sheets.run
step run/show
step run/show/for row in rows

line entry > run call
line Sheet·sheet > run value
known #128 line Sheet·sheet > run/show value     # `print(title, ..)`, the title of the sheet: the reader gives no use of `title`, of no type of the code's
line Sheet·sheet > run/show/for row in rows value          # `rows` holds `sheet.rows`
line run/show/for row in rows > Row·row@run/show/for row in rows value
line Row·row@run/show/for row in rows > run/show value     # `row.text`
line run/show > Screen own

home Sheet·sheet run
home Row·row@run/show/for row in rows run/show

side entry left
side Screen right
